    "introduction": "Howden Joinery supplies kitchens, joinery products and related equipment primarily to trade customers through its Howdens depot network. Builders and installers buy products for their own projects, making local availability, service and relationships with tradespeople important to the model. The company combines product sourcing and manufacturing with distribution through depots that hold stock close to customers. Revenue comes from kitchens and associated items rather than charging homeowners directly for a full installation service. Demand is linked to renovation and construction activity. Product design, depot productivity and supply-chain efficiency influence performance, alongside the ability to offer tradespeople reliable access to complete kitchen solutions.",
